01–03 | Learn a method and practice it
  --------------------------------------

  https://github.com/vatsalp117/build-interactive-study-guides # Transcript + screenshots → offline interactive guide. Labels inferred steps in on-screen demos.

  https://github.com/kangarooking/cangjie-skill # Methods from books, talks, or podcasts → reusable agent skills. Tests when each method applies.

  https://github.com/lowwwbank/anything-to-course # Source material → practice course. Attempt first → worked example → contrasting case → retry.


  04–08 | Take notes and remember what you learn
  ----------------------------------------------

  https://github.com/syuan03/skill-anything # Quizzes and flashcards by section, even for long sources. Exact source quotes carry over to Anki.

  https://github.com/onepathtofreedom/smart-notes-skill # Merges recurring concepts into linked Obsidian notes. Flashcards test connections across lectures.

  https://github.com/baney75/myelinate # Video tutor that asks what you remember before recapping. Timestamped questions point to the clip worth replaying.

  https://github.com/anatoledms/lecture-transcript-to-notes # Captions → Markdown walkthrough. Flags missing demo steps and verifies the lecturer’s references.

  https://github.com/kaixiad/retaincraft # Five study methods with effect sizes from Donoghue & Hattie’s 2021 meta-analysis (242 studies, ~169k participants). FSRS-5 schedules reviews.


  09–12 | Ask better questions and test your understanding
  --------------------------------------------------------

  https://github.com/hkuds/deeptutor # Course-wide Q&A with page citations. Graded questions from your study path become a reusable practice bank.

  https://github.com/janestreet/agent_skills/ # Jane Street’s Socratic oral exam. One question at a time, with a 0–5 mastery map for each subskill.

  https://github.com/vitalysim/the-knowledge-guy # Ask several books one question. Chapter citations show where authors agree, add detail, or disagree.

  https://gist.github.com/suvojit-0x55aa/61053bd8c0b79a1b4f208272778e0247 # Four-pass Feynman prompt for a paper, document, or codebase. Explain it → map it → unpack it → rebuild it.


  13–15 | Quick reference, focused drills, and course design
  ----------------------------------------------------------

  https://github.com/virgiliojr94/book-to-skill # Technical book → chapter lookup, glossary, and decision tables. Loads just the chapter you need.

  https://github.com/mbjornson/feynman # One-concept teach-back. Scores your explanation 1–10 and drills only the gaps until you reach 9/10.

  https://github.com/biswarupbiswas/lecture-notes-skill # Syllabus with CO–PO articulation per NBA SAR. Generates aligned LaTeX/PDF lecture notes, tutorials, and exams.
